odot/pull/112897.patch","merged_at":"2025-11-18T20:03:52Z"},"body":"the current code assumes that float.Parse behaves the same as the internal C++ code, however without using \"end\" as part of the span, it will parse from index 0 to the end of the string, ignoring commas. for example, this causes it to parse \"0,5,0\" with divisor \",\" as [50, 50, 0], as the float.Parse method ignores commas in floats.\r\n\r\nif another divisor is used, it throws a System.FormatException due to containing invalid characters, as it fails to account for the position of the divisor for the span.","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112897/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112897/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null}